items/pthm-cm08-translation.md:115:[F6] Calculus along the motion and translation family ([[thm-chain-rule-for-total-derivatives]], [[thm-algebra-of-derivatives]], [[def-vector-valued-derivative-and-integral]], [[def-euclidean-inner-product]], [[def-interval]], [[cor-zero-derivative-implies-constant]], [[def-ck-euclidean-maps-and-diffeomorphisms]], [[def-jacobian-matrix-and-gradient]], [[def-directional-and-partial-derivatives]]): $J_x$ is an open set containing $0$; each of its interval components is a maximal open interval, and on it $s\mapsto U(t,x+s\xi^a)$ has derivative $\sum_i a\cdot\nabla_{x_i}U(t,x+s\xi^a)$. A $C^1$ function on an interval with zero derivative is constant; openness alone does not connect distinct components.
