items/lem-kam-composed-map-and-derivative-convergence.md:92:6.1 *Limits and sizes.* The bounds of step 4.1 are summable for every fixed angular multi-index, uniformly on $\mathcal L$. Their series therefore define $\Psi_\infty$, with uniform convergence of all angular derivatives. For each label, holomorphic convergence on $S_t$ and Cauchy differentiation prove holomorphy and identify these derivative limits with derivatives of $\Psi_\infty$. Summing the component bounds gives clause 4 after enlarging $A$; decreasing the initial smallness gives $nAE_0\le1/2$. The identity phase map has zero parameter derivative, so summing step 5.1 gives clause 3 for the limit. The parameter increments have summable sizes $2B_j$ and summable Lipschitz constants, yielding $\chi_\infty$, its displacement bound and its asserted Lipschitz bound relative to the identity. [step 4.1, step 5.1, F1, F3, algebra]
