items/prop-cm-oscillator-degenerate-and-repulsive-cases.md:71:1.1 Case $k=0$, $c=0$. [assume-case 1] The model is $mx''=0$. By [F4], $x'$ is a constant $B$ on $J$, and $x(t)-Bt$ has zero derivative, hence is a constant $A$ on $J$. Thus every solution on an arbitrary interval is $A+Bt$, and conversely each such function solves by [F3]. For a global solution the data at zero give $A=x_0$, $B=v_0$. [F1, F3, F4]
