items/pthm-cm11-top-reduction.md:131:[L6] Calculus and algebra: $(R l)'=R'l+Rl'$, $R'=R[\omega]_{\times}$ and $[\omega]_{\times}z=\omega\times z$ for a $C^{1}$ rotation path ([[lem-cm-matrix-curve-derivative-rules]], [[lem-cm-skew-matrix-cross-product-correspondence]], [[def-cm-special-orthogonal-group]]); the cross product is bilinear and alternating with $u\times(u\times w)=(u\cdot w)u-\lVert u\rVert_2^{2}w$ for unit $u$ ([[lem-cross-product-is-bilinear-alternating-and-orthogonal]], [[def-cross-product-in-r3]], [[def-euclidean-inner-product]]); the chain, product and quotient rules hold for the scalar functions below ([[thm-chain-rule-for-total-derivatives]], [[thm-algebra-of-derivatives]], [[def-derivative]], [[def-interval]]); and a continuous real function on an interval with vanishing derivative at every interior point is constant ([[cor-zero-derivative-implies-constant]]).
items/ex-gr-fx11-2.md:188:2.1 At each first-coordinate grid node $x^1_j=2\pi j/N$, [F6] gives $\phi_N(x_j)=1$. The sampled arrays therefore have $h_{ij}=L_*^2\delta_{ij}$, $h^{ik}=L_*^{-2}\delta^{ik}$, $K_{ij}=0$, $\rho=j=\Lambda=0$. Since the discrete derivatives annihilate these constant arrays, the discrete connection and curvature formulas of [F4] give zero; [F4] then gives $\mathcal H_{\boldsymbol\Delta}=\mathcal M_{\boldsymbol\Delta}=0$ at every node. By [F8, F9], each scalar term $|\mathcal H_{\boldsymbol\Delta}(\mathbf j)|^2=|0|^2=0$, and the covector term is zero because $\mathcal M_{\boldsymbol\Delta}=0$. The induced norm of this zero array is therefore zero. The specified piecewise-constant reconstruction of these samples is flat. [given, F3, F4, F6, F8, F9, step 1.1, algebra]
