items/pthm-cm08-general-noether.md:112:[F6] Calculus along the motion ([[thm-chain-rule-for-total-derivatives]], [[thm-algebra-of-derivatives]], [[def-vector-valued-derivative-and-integral]], [[def-euclidean-inner-product]], [[def-interval]], [[cor-zero-derivative-implies-constant]]): composites $t\mapsto\varphi(t,x(t))$ of $C^{1}$ maps with the motion are $C^{1}$ with derivative $D_{t}\varphi$; sums, products and pairings differentiate by the usual rules; a $C^{1}$ real function on an interval is constant if and only if its derivative vanishes everywhere.
items/pthm-em-weak-field-thomson-limit.md:56:about a fixed position $x_0\in\mathbb R^3$. The family time interval $I$ is not required to contain a full period, and no solution $r_\eta$ outside $I$ is assumed. For the periodic-response conclusions (b), (c), impose the following explicit preparation (P): the unique global harmonic-ODE extension of $r_1$ supplied after (a) by [[lem-em-harmonic-forcing-periodic-response]](d), with its actual value and derivative at $0$, is $T$-periodic, $T=2\pi/\omega$. Equivalently its affine drift is zero, or $r_1'(0)=\operatorname{Re}(iw/\omega)$ with $w=(q/m)e\,e^{i\kappa\cdot x_0}$. The linearized equation and affine local/global classification in (a) hold for every stated family even without (P); overlap-only periodicity on a short $I$ is not substituted for (P). Then: (a) [Linearized equation] $\ddot r_1(t)=\frac qmE_{\rm inc}(x_0,t)=\frac qm\operatorname{Re}(e\,e^{i(\kappa\cdot x_0-\omega t)})$ on $I$. (b) [Induced dipole under preparation (P)] $x_0$ is the zeroth-order rest/reference position. Let $a$ be the mean of the global periodic first-order response, so on $I$ one has $r_1=z_p+a$ with $z_p(t)=\operatorname{Re}(-w\omega^{-2}e^{-i\omega t})$. The arbitrary constant $a$ is retained: no exact mean or periodicity of the full nonlinear family is asserted. The oscillating part of the first-order dipole coefficient $q(r_1-a)$ is $\operatorname{Re}(p_0e^{-i\omega t})$ with complex amplitude
