items/thm-fd-global-linear-acoustics.md:48:Assume Countable Choice. Let $d\in\{1,2,3\}$, $\rho_*>0$, $c_*>0$, and let $z_0:\mathbb T^d\to\mathbb R$ and $v_0:\mathbb T^d\to\mathbb R^d$ be smooth periodic data on the normalized torus $\mathbb T^d=(\mathbb R/2\pi\mathbb Z)^d$. Use normalized measure $d\mu=(2\pi)^{-d}dx$, coefficients $\widehat f(k)=\int f(x)e^{-ik\cdot x}\,d\mu(x)$, weights $w_k=(1+|k|^2)^{1/2}$, and componentwise norms $\|f\|_{H^m}^2=\sum_{k\in\mathbb Z^d}w_k^{2m}|\widehat f(k)|^2$. To define the tangent system, let $P:(0,\infty)\to\mathbb R$ be any $C^2$ function with $P^{\prime}(\rho_*)=c_*^2$ (for example, $P(\rho)=c_*^2\rho$). The base nonlinear equations are $\rho_t+\operatorname{div}(\rho u)=0$ and $u_t+u\cdot\nabla u+\rho^{-1}\nabla P(\rho)=0$, for smooth positive scalar $\rho$ and vector $u$ on spacetime. The equilibrium is $(\rho,u)=(\rho_*,0)$. By its tangent system we mean that the derivative at $\epsilon=0$ of each equation residual evaluated at $(\rho,u)=(\rho_*+\epsilon z,\epsilon v)$ vanishes; the perturbation fields are arbitrary smooth maps, and $\epsilon$ is restricted near zero on each compact time interval so that density stays positive. The resulting constant-coefficient tangent system
