items/lem-sr-connecting-field-stretching.md:136:4.2 (Born rigidity preserves the material metric exactly.) Suppose $\theta=0$ on the image of the family. Then by step 3.1 $\partial_sG_{IJ}(s,\xi)=0$ for every $(s,\xi)\in J\times B$. Fix $\xi\in B$; the function $s\mapsto G_{IJ}(s,\xi)$ is $C^1$ on the interval $J$ by step 2.2, hence continuous, with zero derivative at every point of $J$, so it is constant on $J$ by [L12]. As $I,J$ and $\xi$ were arbitrary, the entire internal metric $G$ is preserved exactly along each flow line, with arbitrary label separation. [L12, step 2.2, step 3.1]
