items/lem-gr-schwarzschild-timelike-geodesic-reduction.md:119:1.1 (The fields $\partial_0$ and $\partial_\varphi$ are Killing.) For $\xi=\partial_0$ the lowered field is $\xi_b=g_{0b}=-f\delta^0_b$, and the Killing equation reads $\partial_ag_{0b}+\partial_bg_{0a}-2\Gamma^c{}_{ab}g_{0c}=0$; substituting [L1], the only potentially nonzero components are $(a,b)=(0,1)$: $\partial_1g_{00}+2f\Gamma^0{}_{01}=-f'+f'=0$, and $(a,b)=(0,0)$: $2\partial_0g_{00}=0$; all other components involve derivatives of vanishing components or vanishing symbols, so they vanish. For $\xi=\partial_\varphi$ the lowered field is $\xi_b=r^2\sin^2\vartheta\,\delta^3_b$, and the equation is $\partial_ag_{3b}+\partial_bg_{3a}-2r^2\sin^2\vartheta\,\Gamma^3{}_{ab}=0$; its potentially nonzero components are $(a,b)=(1,3)$: $2r\sin^2\vartheta-2r^2\sin^2\vartheta\cdot(1/r)=0$, $(a,b)=(2,3)$: $2r^2\sin\vartheta\cos\vartheta-2r^2\sin^2\vartheta\cdot\cot\vartheta=0$, and $(a,b)=(3,3)$: $2\partial_3g_{33}=0$; all other components vanish. Hence both fields are Killing by [L2], and $e=-g(U,\partial_0)$ and $\ell=g(U,\partial_\varphi)$ are constant along $\gamma$. For positivity: $n=f^{-1/2}\partial_0$ is a future unit timelike field by [L5], and $-g(n,U)>0$; since $-g(n,U)=f^{-1/2}e$, we get $e>0$. This proves (a). [L1, L2, L5, algebra]
