items/pthm-tgr-gravitating-entropy-criticality.md:41:Assume the model preparation [[post-tgr-gravitating-entropy-variational-preparation]], including a positive even $C^2$ profile pair with compact state-chart range, fixed $R>0$, $b\ge b_*>0$, fixed constraints $E,N_b$, and boundary normalization $\phi(R)=\tfrac12\log b(R)$. Use the exact $\mathrm{ZF}+\mathrm{AC}_\omega$ convention of [[thm-tgr-constrained-entropy-tov-criticality]]. An admissible profile curve is $C^1$ in the sup-norm space $C^0([0,R])^2$ on an open interval about zero, takes values in the even $C^2$ positive-b profile domain with range in a compact subset of the open state chart, and has a smooth derivative at zero compactly supported in $(0,R)$ and extended evenly at the center. Define constrained stationarity to mean that $S$ has zero derivative at the base profile along every such curve preserving both $E$ and $N_b$. Then constrained stationarity is equivalent to the existence of constants $\alpha,\Theta_K,\mu_K$ such that on $(0,R)$
items/texp-em-displacement-current-surface-choice.md:181:2.2 For (c), the graphs $r_1(u,v)=(u,v,-2\eta(u,v))$ and $r_2(u,v)=(u,v,0)$ have parameter derivatives with cross products $r_{1,u}\times r_{1,v}=(2\eta_u,2\eta_v,1)$ and $r_{2,u}\times r_{2,v}=e_z$, both nonzero on the interior of $D$; the boundary chains take values $(u,v,0)$ on $\partial D$ for both, so they coincide, and the region $V=\{(u,v,w):(u,v)\in D^\circ,-2\eta(u,v)<w<0\}$ is bounded, open, nonempty, and has exactly the two graph faces with outward normals $-n_1$ and $+n_2$ off the square seam, which is a finite union of line segments of surface measure zero; thus the presentation hypotheses of [F2] are met. The oriented flux formula gives $\int_{S_1}J\cdot n_1\,dS=\int_D(J\circ r_1)\cdot(r_{1,u}\times r_{1,v})\,dudv=-\int_D\chi(-2\eta(u,v))\,dudv$ and $\int_{S_2}J\cdot n_2\,dS=-\int_D\chi(0)\,dudv=0$. On $Q_0=[-1/2,1/2]^2$ we have $\eta=1$ and $\chi(-2\eta)=1$. The integrand is nonnegative on $D$; cutting $D$ along the four sides of $Q_0$, coordinate-slice additivity and monotonicity [F5] give $\int_D\chi(-2\eta)\ge\int_{Q_0}1=1$, where the constant integral is its constant Darboux-sum value. Hence the first flux is strictly negative, while the second vanishes; the total fluxes vanish because $G=J+\varepsilon_0\partial_tE=-\chi(z)e_z+\chi(z)e_z=0$, consistently with $\oint_\gamma B\cdot d\mathbf r=0$. [F4, F5, F6, step 1.2, given, algebra]
