items/lem-fd-transport-and-density.md:133:10.1 Set $R:=D_t\rho+\rho\theta$. It is continuous on $\Omega$ because $u,\rho\in C^1$ and $\theta$ is continuous. Step 9.1 gives $M_K'(t)=\int_{\chi_t(K)}R(t,x)\,dx$. If $R=0$, each $M_K$ has zero derivative and is constant by [F10] on $I$. [F10, step 9.1, given]
