+          "fact": "F3",
+          "source": "def-derivative",
+          "source_section": "Definition",
+          "quote": "$f$ is **differentiable at $c$** when that limit exists, and then the **derivative of $f$ at $c$** is $$f'(c) \\;:=\\; \\lim_{x \\to c} q_{f,c}(x) \\;=\\; \\lim_{x \\to c} \\frac{f(x) - f(c)}{x - c} .$$",
+          "uses": ["3.1"]
+        },
+        {
+          "fact": "F4",
+          "source": "cor-zero-derivative-implies-constant",
+          "source_section": "Statement",
+          "quote": "Then $f$ is constant on $I$: there is a real $k$ with $f(x) = k$ for every $x \\in I$.",
+          "uses": ["3.1"]
+        }
+      ],
